Ours.  Key repeat comes from one place: XKB's RepeatKeys when XKB is on,
the DDX's own repeat only when the server runs with -kb (XKB off), as
the shipped display configuration does.

- The DDX repeat replaced the server's select timeout from its block
  handler, so a shorter timeout of the server's was lost; it now only
  shortens it, to the time left before the next repeat;
- tvplus left tv_usec at 1000000 unnormalised, and -ar1 1000 or more gave
  an EINVAL select that spun the server: the timeout is computed in
  microseconds and normalised, and -ar1/-ar2 are bounded to 1..30000 ms;
- it ignored `xset r off` for single keys: a key repeats only when its
  autoRepeats bit is set;
- with XKB on both repeated, doubling every repeat; -ar1/-ar2 now reach
  XKB as well (read here, not consumed);
- the system's own repeat events (qualifier REPEAT) are dropped.

--- a/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/amix.h
+++ b/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/amix.h
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@
 #define tvplus(tv, tv1, tv2)	/* tv = tv1 + tv2 */ \
 		(tv).tv_sec = (tv1).tv_sec + (tv2).tv_sec; \
 		(tv).tv_usec = (tv1).tv_usec + (tv2).tv_usec; \
-		if ((tv).tv_usec > 1000000) { \
+		if ((tv).tv_usec >= 1000000) { \
 			(tv).tv_usec -= 1000000; \
 			(tv).tv_sec += 1; \
 		}
